From: OpenWrt WR11000 port
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: keep the regd when a reg event has no rules

On IPQ5332 + QCN9274 (Cudy WR11000) the firmware answers a country
request with status PASS and zero regulatory rules (seen for alpha2
"00"; see also 991-wifi-ath12k-track-country-sent-to-firmware.patch).
ath12k_pull_reg_chan_list_ext_update_ev() treats that as a parse error,
so ath12k_reg_chan_list_event() ends in its fallback path and hits
WARN_ON(1) - the "rare, TODO" case meant for firmware and host
disagreeing about an applied regd. Every boot logs one stack trace per
radio:

  ath12k_wifi7_ahb c000000.wifi: No reg rules available
  ath12k_wifi7_ahb c000000.wifi: failed to extract regulatory info from received event
  WARNING: ... at drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c:7097 ath12k_wmi_op_rx

The check also runs before phy_id is parsed, so the event's radio is
unknown and its regd_update_completed is never signalled.

Do the zero-rules check after the event header is parsed and return
-ENODATA for it. The caller keeps the current regd, as for a dropped
event, which is what already happened before minus the WARN, and still
completes regd_update_completed for that radio.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
@@ -6076,11 +6076,6 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (!total_reg_rules) {
-		ath12k_warn(ab, "No reg rules available\n");
-		return -EINVAL;
-	}
-
 	memcpy(reg_info->alpha2, &ev->alpha2, REG_ALPHA2_LEN);
 
 	reg_info->dfs_region = le32_to_cpu(ev->dfs_region);
@@ -6111,6 +6106,17 @@
 		break;
 	}
 
+	/* Checked only now, so the caller still learns which radio the event
+	 * was for: some firmware answers a country request with no rules at
+	 * all (seen for alpha2 "00" on IPQ5332 and QCN9274, status PASS).
+	 */
+	if (!total_reg_rules) {
+		ath12k_info(ab, "no reg rules for alpha2 %c%c (phy %u, status %u), keeping current regd\n",
+			    reg_info->alpha2[0], reg_info->alpha2[1],
+			    reg_info->phy_id, le32_to_cpu(ev->status_code));
+		return -ENODATA;
+	}
+
 	reg_info->is_ext_reg_event = true;
 
 	reg_info->min_bw_2g = le32_to_cpu(ev->min_bw_2g);
@@ -7031,6 +7037,17 @@
 	}
 
 	ret = ath12k_pull_reg_chan_list_ext_update_ev(ab, skb, reg_info);
+	if (ret == -ENODATA) {
+		/* Firmware applied the request but sent nothing to build a
+		 * regd from. Keep the current one, as for a dropped event:
+		 * this is not the "firmware and host disagree" case the
+		 * fallback WARN is for. Still signal the completion that
+		 * ath12k_mac_hw_register() may be waiting on.
+		 */
+		pdev_idx = reg_info->phy_id;
+		ret = ATH12K_REG_STATUS_VALID;
+		goto mem_free;
+	}
 	if (ret) {
 		ath12k_warn(ab, "failed to extract regulatory info from received event\n");
 		goto mem_free;
